<title>UK: BOE revises money market shortage to 2.0 bln stg.</title>
<headline>BOE revises money market shortage to 2.0 bln stg.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England said it had revised its forecast money market shortage to 2.0 billion stg from 1.9 billion.</p>
<p>That leaves a residual shortage of 1.239 billion stg, following earlier assistance.</p>
<p>The Bank invited fixed rate operations comprising repos to May 6 and 7 and outright offers of bills maturing on or before May 7.</p>
